===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|artificial intelligence}} A [[real]] or [[virtual]] [[computer]] [[system]] designed to [[emulate]] the [[brain]] in its [[ability]] to "[[learn]]" to [[assess]] [[imprecise]] [[data]].
#: {{hypo|en|large language model}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=UN Study: China, US, Japan Lead World AI Development|url=https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/un-study-china-us-japan-lead-world-ai-development/4769094.html|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190207184548/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/un-study-china-us-japan-lead-world-ai-development/4769094.html|archivedate=7 February 2019|work={{w|Voice of America}}|date=3 February 2019|passage=A '''neural network''' is a computer system built to simulate, or act like, the human brain.}}
#*:: {{audio|en|A neural network is a computer system built to simulate, or act like, the human brain.ogg|Audio (US)}}
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Any network of [[neuron]]s etc., that [[function]] [[together]] to achieve a common purpose.
#: {{hypo|en|artificial neural network|simulated neural network}}

